@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] editor-broker-trusted-preface
The guest broker MUST accept only the exact Lilly gateway on the guest's fixed
eth0 address and port 4444. A bounded, closed, boot-bound account preface and
current account reconciliation MUST precede worker startup or forwarding bytes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] editor-worker-account-custody
Linux editor workers MUST run as the ensured account in independent systemd units.
Runtime directories MUST have mode 0700, sockets mode 0600, and accepted Unix
connections MUST have the expected kernel peer UID. The broker MUST NOT launch
a shell, construct caller-controlled executable paths or relay authentication
preface fields into editor HTTP requests.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] editor-all-workspaces-trusted
Every editor worker MUST pass the upstream disable-workspace-trust flag so all
folders are trusted, including outside HOME and under conflicting personal
settings. Per-user trust storage MUST NOT be required for editor startup.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] editor-worker-independent-lifetime
A Linux guest broker restart MUST NOT stop editor workers or delete their runtime
directories. Readiness MUST inspect the existing socket, kernel peer UID, source
commit and root systemd launch identity for the exact UID/name, protocol, commit,
release and origin before reusing a worker. A mismatched legitimate worker MUST
be stopped successfully before recreation, preserving personal files; metadata
failure and foreign socket custody MUST refuse without stopping that worker.
Startup MUST be single-flight per account. Upstream grace and
shutdown behavior MUST retire idle workers without an independent broker timer.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] editor-broker-closed-diagnostics
Broker diagnostics MUST contain only fixed event and reason enums. They MUST NOT
contain incoming frames, paths, account identities, origins, arguments or bytes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] windows-editor-staging-custody
The separate Windows launcher library MUST bind a validated current execution,
package and canonical roster account to its current local SAM SID. S4U tokens,
worker processes and named-pipe servers MUST match that exact SID. Processes
MUST join a SYSTEM-only named job while suspended; broker handle closure MUST
NOT stop resumed workers. Reuse MUST verify process creation time, executable,
job ownership/membership and pipe server PID. Unknown or foreign custody MUST
refuse without terminating processes or deleting personal files. Library
presence MUST NOT enable an image capability or a network listener.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] windows-editor-boot-receipt-lifetime
Receipts MUST live in a SYSTEM-only namespace derived from the validated MMDS
physical boot challenge, placement and epoch. A renewed session/generation MAY
reuse only the exact validated stable worker identity in that same namespace.
Prior boot receipts MUST NOT authorize current workers. Every new launch MUST
publish a complete private receipt or stop its entire owned job; failed cleanup
MUST surface. Recovery of a conclusively absent retained root process MUST stop
any remaining proven SYSTEM-owned exact-job descendants before replacement;
PID reuse and incomplete or foreign custody MUST refuse cleanup.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] windows-editor-platform-path-authority
Worker PATH MUST be a bounded explicit list of distinct ASCII absolute local
directories with native owner, write-ACL and reparse custody. SYSTEM and
Administrators MAY control package leaves. The exact Windows TrustedInstaller
service SID MAY additionally control PATH directories and directory ancestors,
because platform servicing already controls the OS executable environment;
foreign owners and foreign replacement/delete/ACL authority MUST refuse.
TrustedInstaller MUST NOT authorize package leaves or SYSTEM-only state.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] windows-editor-overlapped-pipe
The Windows named pipe MUST be opened with overlapped I/O and each read or
write MUST have bounded kernel waits. A healthy idle relay MUST wait for bytes
or explicit shutdown without an idle read deadline, polling cancellation at
most every 100ms; blocked writes MUST retain their bounded deadline. A timed-out
or cancelled operation MUST be cancelled and
retain owned OVERLAPPED storage, copied buffer and handles until a nonblocking
drain observes completion. Kernel I/O MUST NOT reference caller storage after
return. Live and pending cancelled operations MUST share at most 128 pipe
reservations, acquired before open/duplication; exhaustion MUST refuse new
pipes. At most one process-wide completion reaper may run. A broker request
thread MUST NOT remain blocked on a worker pipe after worker loss.
